  "notes": "Built from archived 2024-2025 bulletin (https://bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2024-2025/undergraduate/colleges/arts-architecture/art-ba/). That bulletin page publishes only a GENERIC Art, B.A. suggested plan (\"Additional Course for Major (see list)\" and \"Supporting Course for Concentration\" slots, total 120cr) -- it does not print a concentration-specific table, in this or any other archive year checked (2022-23 through the current 2026-27 edition all use the identical generic template). This plan instantiates one concrete path through that generic framework using the Drawing and Painting concentration (prescribed foundations ART 11/110/111/122Y/ARTH 111/112, plus specific studio picks for the \"Additional Course\" and \"Supporting Course for Concentration\" slots), matching the bulletin's own 120cr total. AUDIT FIX (reviewer #2): two course codes among the specific studio picks did not exist in the real PSU course catalog or the university course-description pages -- \"ART 420\" (Semester 6) and \"ART 445\" (Semester 7, alternate to ART 496) were not real courses under any department. Replaced with ART 350 (Intermediate Painting) and ART 450 (Advanced Painting), both real, catalogued, and consistent with the Drawing and Painting concentration theme. Flagging for follow-up (left as-is, out of audit scope): the plan also carries ART 240/ART 340 (Beginning Printmaking/Printmaking) in a plan labeled \"Drawing and Painting\" concentration, and three real studio courses (ART 320, ART 340, ART 440) are listed at 3cr where the catalog lists them at 4cr -- both predate this audit pass; changing the credit values would shift the plan's total away from the bulletin's own 120cr, so a future pass should reconcile these against the department's own (not published in the bulletin) per-concentration course list.",
